From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 05:39:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Track which request an <img> is waiting on

A src/srcset mutation re-runs load_image, which either applies a cached
image synchronously (no delivery notification) or starts a fetch
(delivery notification later). An embedder DOM may mark the <img>
pending-reload on every mutation, but for the synchronous cache-hit path
no notification ever clears the flag, so HTMLImageElement.complete
sticks false forever. That breaks React components polling img.complete
post-hydration (BBC's Image placeholder never unmounts and paints over
the real image).

node_has_pending_image lets the JS side ask, right after the mutation,
whether a fetch is actually underway for the node. The embedder can't
answer this itself: srcset candidate selection lives in the mutator
(select_image_url) and the embedder doesn't know which URL blitz picked.

load_image added the node to the new URL's pending list but never took
it off the previous one. Both responses then targeted it, and the first
to land won: a stale success painted the old image over the new src, and
a stale 404 reported the node broken. An embedder that keeps the first
terminal state per node also lost the real load event to that 404 (WPT
img.complete.html "async src complete test").

Drop the node's Image entries from every pending list before queueing
the new request. The old fetch stays in flight and still fills the image
cache.
---
 src/document.rs | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 src/mutator.rs  | 10 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/document.rs b/src/document.rs
index 4780ad6..45f8e57 100644
--- a/src/document.rs
+++ b/src/document.rs
@@ -1643,6 +1643,22 @@ impl BaseDocument {
             .unwrap_or_default()
     }

+    /// Whether `node_id` is currently waiting on an
+    /// in-flight image fetch (any URL). Complements image_cache_has
+    /// for the srcset case: the JS side can't re-run candidate
+    /// selection, so after a src/srcset mutation it asks whether
+    /// load_image actually started a fetch. Not pending = the
+    /// mutation reached a terminal state synchronously (cache-hit
+    /// apply, or no fetchable candidate) and no delivery
+    /// notification will ever fire.
+    pub fn node_has_pending_image(&self, node_id: NodeId) -> bool {
+        self.pending_images.values().any(|waiting| {
+            waiting
+                .iter()
+                .any(|(id, ty)| *id == node_id && matches!(ty, ImageType::Image))
+        })
+    }
+
     pub fn load_resource(&mut self, res: ResourceLoadResponse) {
         self.pending_critical_resources.remove(&res.request_id);

diff --git a/src/mutator.rs b/src/mutator.rs
index 2c83b80..7ac9223 100644
--- a/src/mutator.rs
+++ b/src/mutator.rs
@@ -1453,6 +1453,16 @@ impl<'doc> DocumentMutator<'doc> {
     }

     fn load_image(&mut self, target_id: NodeId) {
+        // An <img> waits on its latest request only. Changing
+        // src left the node queued under the previous URL too, so
+        // whichever response landed first won: a stale success painted
+        // the old image, and a stale 404 reported the node broken (the
+        // shim keeps the first terminal state), swallowing the real
+        // load event (WPT img.complete.html "async src complete test").
+        // The old fetch stays in flight and still fills the cache.
+        for waiting in self.doc.pending_images.values_mut() {
+            waiting.retain(|(id, ty)| !(*id == target_id && matches!(ty, ImageType::Image)));
+        }
         if let Some(raw_src) = self.select_image_url(target_id) {
             if !raw_src.is_empty() {
                 // Fallible resolve. `img.src = "http://"`
